<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 157,600 tonnes wheat, 22,400 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 157,600 tonnes wheat, 22,400 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it had bought 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 57,600 of Canadian wheat and 40,000 of Australian wheat at its weekly tender, all for December shipment.</p>
<p>It also bought 20,000 tonnes of U.S. barley and 2,400 of Canadian barley.</p>
<p>The tender results details are as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 60,000	   Western white	    20,000</p>
<p>				   Dark northern spring   25,000</p>
<p>				   Hard red winter</p>
<p>				   (11.5 percent protein) 15,000</p>
<p> Canada     57,600	   1 Canadian western red spring</p>
<p>								  57,600</p>
<p> Australia  40,000	   Standard white	   20,000</p>
<p>				   Prime Hard		 20,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p> Country    Quantity</p>
<p> U.S.	 20,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
<p> Canada	2,400	   Food			  2,400</p>
</text>
